{% extends "layouts/docs" %}

{% block content %}
	<p>Kiln is built to run templates written by other people, such as editors in a CMS or AI agents. A template can only read what you give it, and limits stop templates that would run for too long.</p>

	<h2>What templates can read</h2>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Plain objects:</strong> their own properties only. Nothing inherited from <code>Object.prototype</code>.</li>
		<li><strong>Arrays:</strong> items by index, and <code>length</code>.</li>
		<li><strong>Strings:</strong> no properties. Use filters such as <code>length</code> instead.</li>
		<li><strong>Class instances:</strong> only the members their class <a href="/docs/api/safe-markup/#class-instances">exposes</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>Never:</strong> <code>constructor</code>, <code>prototype</code> or <code>__proto__</code>, even when they are an object's own properties.</li>
	</ul>

	<p>Templates can only call functions you registered, the built-ins, macros, their own arrow functions and exposed methods. A function stored in your data can't be called.</p>

	<h2>Limits</h2>

	<p>Every render has limits. Exceeding one stops the render with an error.</p>

	<table>
		<thead><tr><th>Limit</th><th>Default</th><th>What it counts</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td><code>maxOutputLength</code></td><td>5,000,000</td><td>Characters of output</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>maxSteps</code></td><td>1,000,000</td><td>Tags, outputs, loop passes and calls</td></tr>
			<tr><td><code>maxDepth</code></td><td>64</td><td>Nested includes, components, macro calls and layouts</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	{% apply highlight("ts") %}
		{% verbatim %}
const kiln = createKiln({
	loader,
	limits: { maxSteps: 200_000, maxDepth: 32 },
});
		{% endverbatim %}
	{% endapply %}

	<p>Built-in filters count the items they process, so one call to <code>sort</code> or <code>merge</code> can't do unlimited work.</p>

	<p>Pass an <code>AbortSignal</code> as the <code>signal</code> render option to stop a render from outside, for example when the visitor disconnects. On Cloudflare Workers, the platform's CPU limit is a final backstop.</p>

	<h2>Other safeguards</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Output is <a href="/docs/language/escaping/">escaped</a> by default.</li>
		<li>Templates can't build regular expressions, so they can't cause slow pattern matching.</li>
		<li>Templates can't compile other templates from strings.</li>
		<li>Kiln never generates code while rendering. <a href="/docs/api/precompiling/">Precompiled templates</a> are JavaScript you build and ship, so only precompile templates you trust.</li>
		<li><code>dump</code> outputs nothing unless you turn on <code>debug</code>.</li>
		<li>A failed render returns no partial output.</li>
	</ul>
{% endblock %}
